Here at Sony Music Entertainment, we are shaping what’s next in a way that creates impact. Forging powerful new ideas at the heart of music, technology, and culture that entertain and move people. &nbsp;

This is your opportunity. Part of a global community, united by individual passion, rising to that challenge every day. Adapting at pace and supporting one another, inspired to influence the future. For the benefit of you, our people; our creators, our business, and wider society too.&nbsp;This is your chance to shape your impact on Sony Music and beyond.

The Design team is part of 4th Floor Creative and works with all of Sony’s labels to conceptualise, design and develop creative artwork concepts for artist campaigns. The design team also contribute to other 4th Floor projects across brands, CRM, digital initiatives and the Podcast division. Working in a fast-moving and lively environment, you will be accountable for designing digital artwork, branding, presentations and other marketing collateral, including some print packaging. You will need to be dedicated to producing high quality work and have a great eye for detail. The right candidate will be passionate about contemporary visual culture, fashion, photography and typography.

You must submit a portfolio as part of your application for this role.&nbsp;

Please note: This application form cannot be saved part-way through. We recommend preparing your answers in a separate document and then copying them into the form when you’re ready to submit. If you’d like to take additional time to complete your application, please ensure you gather your responses externally before submitting in one go.&nbsp;

If you have any reasonable adjustment requests, please reach out to recruitment.support@sonymusic.com.&nbsp;

Role Overview:

Ways of Working

• Office attendance: Monday to Thursday

• Offsite working: Occasional off-site event attendance required

What you'll do:

• Designing treatments, pitch documents and internal communications

• Art direction &amp; Design for print and digital assets across Sony artist campaigns and wider 4th Floor initiatives. Including, though not exclusively, logos, single / album / EP artwork, digital assets, and merch

• Layout &amp; design for CD and vinyl formats

• Liaise with the Visual Creative team and other stakeholders to ensure delivery of creative is prioritised and on time

• Keep up to date with the latest design and tech developments

• Participate in creative sessions alongside the Visual Creative team, marketing managers, artist managers and other stakeholders&nbsp;

Who you are:

Essential

• Competent in Adobe Creative suite

• Love of all visual culture

• Cinema 4D or similar experience

Nice to have

• Someone with a self-starter mentality and approach

• Can do attitude, resilient

• A team player and someone comfortable working in a group

• Any other creative outlets or interests&nbsp;

What we give you:

• An annual salary of £28,480 (London Living Wage)

• You join a vibrant global community with the opportunity to channel your passion every day &nbsp;

• A modern office environment designed for you, empowering you to bring your best &nbsp;

• Investment in your professional growth and development such as focused workshops and a dedicated mentor, enabling you to thrive in our vibrant community&nbsp; &nbsp;

• The space to accelerate progress, positively disrupt and create what happens next &nbsp;

• We give you the platform to champion positive change, with the opportunity to contribute to our social impact, diversity, equity and inclusion initiatives &nbsp;

• We provide an excellent range of benefits like private medical cover, a generous pension scheme, life assurance, income protection, plus loads of music industry perks. There’s also time off over winter break &nbsp;

