We are WPP Production - the unified global production company that brings together all of WPP's content producers, studios and craft experts into one connected organisation. We combine world-class human craft with next generation technology to originate, design, and deliver multi-channel content systems at scale. Built for borderless collaboration and powered by deep craft expertise, we are the production engine designed for today's always on, AI driven marketing world.

About WPP

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&nbsp;in a single company -&nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&nbsp; WPP.com .

A Hybrid working model

We believe the best work happens when we're together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That's why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.

What does a Campaign Manager do at WPP Production? &nbsp;

Our Campaign Managers (CMs) are super-organised and adept multi-taskers. They are accountable for end-to-end project delivery, delivering projects on time, on specification and on budget.   &nbsp;Our CMs possess good project and client management skills and best-practice&nbsp;methodology. They are the key contact for projects, responsible for relaying timing, scope, budget, resource and change information to the wider project and production teams.    &nbsp;

Due to an increased volume of work coming in from the client, we are opening an opportunity to work on one of the world’s most recognised luxury brands. &nbsp;

To thrive in this role, you will be highly organised with a passion for delivering top tier client service and have a strong personal desire to continually grow and develop your skills.   You’ll&nbsp;be experienced in client servicing and have a background in localisation of moving picture and digital banners.&nbsp; &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Reporting lines and key stakeholders &nbsp;

This role reports into a Senior Campaign Manager. &nbsp;

There will be close collaboration with all teams across the client account including a network of freelancers and other agencies the client appoints for&nbsp;different stages&nbsp;of their advertising materials production. &nbsp;

 

